mes a `:global` name obligation. This is a deliberate execution-contract change from today's `(zipmap params args)` fallback. Therefore, name obligations are strictly and statically the set of `:global` names, never `:variable` indices.\n+**Variables never fall through to globals.** An under-arity call leaves missing parameter names bound to `nil`; an over-arity call drops extra arguments beyond the params list length. An unbound variable name evaluates to `nil`; it never falls through to the store, primitives, or modules (since `:variable` and `:global` are distinct nodes). Therefore, name obligations are strictly and statically the set of `:global` names, never `:variable` names.\n \n Every retained obligation is a required primitive or module export, checked by\n profile (UCF §7.5.2), and the **effects of a callable are read from its\n@@ -1732,15 +1732,15 @@ rows behind it. The semantics do not change; the boundary does.\n +--------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n | linearizer,                                      | reads the row relation through the same `get-attr`-over-an-index shape it has today (`lower-node`'s `(get-attr e    |\n | `linearize.cljc:87-148`,                         | :yin/type)` becomes a lookup by row id); `ast-children` becomes a table lookup of `node`/`nodes` slot positions;    |\n-| `:230-242`                                       | `lower` takes a row set and returns a vector plus the §5.3 provenance table; emits `:var index`, `:global name`, and `:closure arity body`; `lower-ast` (`:245-252`) goes away     |\n+| `:230-242`                                       | `lower` takes a row set and returns a vector plus the §5.3 provenance table; emits `:var name`, `:global name`, and `:closure params body`; `lower-ast` (`:245-252`) goes away     |\n +--------------------------------------------------+-----------------